n seat: Tina Smith (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's open Senate seat, held by Democrats since 2008, features Lieutenant Governor Peggy Flanagan against former broadcaster Michele Tafoya after Tina Smith's retirement. The state leans Democratic by about three points, and polls throughout October have shown Flanagan ahead, though by margins ranging from three points in Republican-leaning surveys to fourteen in the New York Times/Siena poll. Outside groups have spent heavily against Flanagan, and Tafoya has kept pace financially, raising $12.5 million.\n\nExpert raters mostly call the race Likely Democratic, with several at Lean Democratic, and prediction markets price Flanagan's chances above ninety percent. The consistent polling lead, the state's partisan lean, and a favorable national environment all point to a Democratic hold, though the spread among pollsters leaves some room for a closer finish.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8725, "margin": 5.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7776, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8131, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8217, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7867, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.784, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7719, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7956, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7935, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7758, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8073, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7878, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7863, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.738, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7059, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7067, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.8031, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.7655, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.7895, "mar